      "username": "Reckless",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
      "created_at": "2013-05-04T17:06:41.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"imprimis5\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/imprimis5/48/2387_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> imprimis5:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Full disclosure: I haven't played with anything but three sectors.There's a lot going on with three sectors to keep track of. Not only that, but the thinner you spread your ships, the harder the game gets (at least, that's my opinion). It seems that adding another sector not only complicates things significantly more, but it would make things much harder strategically.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Agreed.&nbsp; Setting up for three sectors consistently makes for a pretty strategic and challenging game.&nbsp; I think if it got up to four or five the game would be much more complicated and would take a lot of the fun out of it.</p>",
